  "comments": "<p>Difference between normal and wide rim:<br><a href=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/63e690bd9d370.jpg\"><img src=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/miniatures/63e690bd9d370.jpg\" alt=\"\"></a></p><p><strong>Hórreos</strong> are raised granaries found in the northwest Iberian peninsula made to keep rodents out.</p><p>Cruz de la Victoria, c.908, emblema of Asturias, see:</p><p><a href=\"https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Victory_Cross\" rel=\"ugc noopener\" target=\"_blank\" >https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Victory_Cross</a><br><strong>Asturias</strong>, officially the Principality of Asturias, is an autonomous community in northwest Spain. It is coextensive with the province of Asturias and contains some of the territory that was part of the larger Kingdom of Asturias in the Middle Ages. Divided into eight comarcas (counties), the autonomous community of Asturias is bordered by Cantabria to the east, by León (Castile and León) to the south, by Lugo (Galicia) to the west, and by the Cantabrian sea to the north.</p>",
